The root account should only be used for administrational purposes. For everyday
tasks, a user account with restricted privileges should be used.

Each user receives a personal folder in /home. This folder and all files
contained within have write and read permissions restricted to the user that
owns the folder. For each user a login shell may also be specified. This is the
shell that will be started upon the user's login. On a system with multiple
users it makes sense to create individual accounts for each.
